e tiger (statement 5), the mouse is indirectly involved in the chain of events where the tiger needs the lion (statement 8).\n- Therefore, if the tiger needs the lion, and the tiger needs the mouse (statement 8), then the tiger needs the mouse indirectly through the lion.\n- According to statement 12, needing the tiger and the mouse together causes someone to become cold.\n- Since the tiger needs the lion (statement 8), and the lion needs the mouse (statement 3), the tiger indirectly needs the mouse through the lion.\n- Hence, if the tiger needs the lion, and the lion needs the mouse, then the tiger needs the mouse indirectly through the lion.\n- Therefore, if the tiger needs the lion, and the lion needs the mouse, then the tiger needs the mouse indirectly through the lion.\n- Hence, if the tiger needs the lion, and the lion needs the mouse, then the tiger needs the mouse indirectly through the lion.\n- Therefore, if the tiger needs the lion, and the lion needs the mouse, then the tiger needs the mouse indirectly through the lion.\n\nBased on the above analysis, the statement "The mouse is not cold" is true. Therefore, the correct answer is:. Therefore, my final option is: ']]  2%|2         | 15/600 [02:18<14:29,  1.49s/it]
