 are green.\n\n12. **If someone is blue then they are green.**.\n    - This statement tells us that if someone is blue, then they are green.\n\n13. **Blue, green people are white.**.\n    - This statement tells us that blue and green people are white.\n\n14. **If Bob is smart and Bob is blue then Bob is not green.**.\n    - This statement tells us that if Bob is smart and blue, then Bob is not green.\n\n15. **If Charlie is white then Charlie is nice.**.\n    - This statement tells us that if Charlie is white, then Charlie is nice.\n\n16. **All white people are smart.**.\n    - This statement tells us that all white people are smart.\n\nNow, let\'s consider the statement "Erin is not smart.".\n\nFrom the information provided, we know:.\n- Erin is nice.\n- All nice people are cold.\n- All cold people are blue.\n- Blue, green people are white.\n- All white people are smart.\n\nSince Erin is nice, she must be cold. And since all cold people are blue, Erin must be blue. Finally, since blue, green people are white, and all white people are smart, Erin must be smart.\n\nTherefore, the statement "Erin is not smart" is false.\n\n<｜User｜>Please solve the logical reasoning problem. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
