rt.\n- From point 11, if someone is smart, they are green.\n- From point 12, if someone is green, they are nice.\n- Therefore, since Dave is smart, he must be green.\n- From point 13, nice people are young.\n- From point 14, if someone is white, they are young.\n- From point 5, Dave is white.\n- Thus, Dave is young.\n- From point 15, if someone is cold, they are white.\n- Since Dave is cold, he must be white.\n- From point 16, if someone is green and smart, they are white.\n- Since Dave is green and smart, he must be white.\n- From point 17, all young, red people are smart.\n- Since Dave is not red, this condition does not apply to him.\n- From point 18, if Fiona is red, she is green.\n- Since Fiona is not red, this condition does not apply to her.\n- From point 19, if Anne is smart, she is not green.\n- Since Anne is nice, she is not green.\n- Since Anne is not green, this condition does not apply to her.\n\nBased on the analysis, Dave is nice because he is green, and green people are nice. Therefore, the statement "Dave is nice" is true.\n\n<｜User｜>Please solve the logical reasoning problem. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
