messages:   16%|#5        | 95/600 [30:58<11:10,  1.33s/it][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nAnne is smart. Charlie is nice. Erin is furry. Erin is white. Fiona is smart. Fiona is white. Fiona is young. Nice, smart things are young. All young, white things are cold. White things are red. All furry, red things are nice. All young things are white. All young things are white. All smart, cold things are furry. If something is nice and white then it is smart. If Anne is furry and Anne is white then Anne is red.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Erin is cold.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown. I think the correct option is: C\n', '<think>\nTo determine whether the statement "Erin is cold" is true, false, or unknown based on the given information, let\'s analyze the information step by step:\n\n1. **Anne is smart.** (Given)\n2. **Charlie is nice.** (Given)\n3. **Erin is furry.** (Given)\n4. **Erin is white.** (Given)\n5. **Fiona is smart.** (Given)\n6. **Fiona is white.** (Given)\n7. **Fiona is young.** (Given)\n8. **Nice, smart things are young.** (Given)\n9. **All young, white things are cold.** (Given)\n10. **White things are red.** (Given)\n11. **All furry, red things are nice.** (Given)\n12. **All young things are white.** (Given)\n13. **All young things are white.** (Given)\n14. **All smart, cold things are furry.** (Given)\n15. **If something is nice and white then it is smart.** (Given)\n16. **If Anne is furry and Anne is white then Anne is red.** (Given)\n\nNow, let\'s examine the statement "Erin is cold" using the provided information:\n\n- Erin is white (from point 3).\n- Since white things are red (point 10), Erin is red.\n- Since all furry, red things are nice (point 11), and Erin is red, Erin must be nice.\n- Since nice, smart things are young (point 8), and Erin is nice, Erin must be young.\n- Since all young, white things are cold (point 9), and Erin is white, Erin must be cold.\n\nTherefore, based on the given information, the statement "Erin is cold" is true.\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
