hing is rough, it must be red.\n15. **All big, red things are cold.** This statement tells us that all big, red things are cold.\n16. **All round things are green.** This statement tells us that all round things are green.\n17. **Round, cold things are big.** This statement tells us that round, cold things are big.\n\nNow, let\'s consider the statement "Dave is big." We need to check if there is any information that directly or indirectly confirms or denies this statement.\n\n- From the given information, we know that Dave is round (statement 6).\n- From statement 16, we know that all round things are big.\n- Therefore, since Dave is round, it follows that Dave is big.\n\nThus, based on the given information, the statement "Dave is big" is true.\n\n<｜User｜>Please solve the logical reasoning problem. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
