, it must also be furry.\n\n10. **If something is big then it is quiet.**.\n    - This means that if an object is big, it must also be quiet.\n\n11. **Quiet things are blue.**.\n    - This means that if an object is quiet, it must also be blue.\n\n12. **Rough things are kind.**.\n    - This means that if an object is rough, it must also be kind.\n\nNow, let\'s consider the statement "Harry is not furry":.\n\n- We know that Harry is big (from statement 10).\n- From statement 11, since Harry is big, it must be quiet.\n- From statement 12, since Harry is quiet, it must be blue.\n- From statement 1, since Harry is blue, it must be rough.\n- From statement 13, since Harry is rough, it must be kind.\n- From statement 9, since Harry is kind, it must be furry.\n\nTherefore, based on the given information, Harry is furry, not not furry. Hence, the statement "Harry is not furry" is false.\n\n<｜User｜>Please solve the logical reasoning problem. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
