 following statement true, false, or unknown? Bob is not blue.\n# Options:.\nA) True.\nB) False.\nC) Unknown<｜Assistant｜>.\nBased on the analysis provided, the correct answer is:.\n\nB) False.\n\nThis is because the context explicitly states that Bob is blue, and there is no information suggesting otherwise. The rule "All white things are blue" confirms that if something is white, it must also be blue. Since Bob is white, he must be blue. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
