h.\n11. **If something is red and nice then it is cold.** - This implies that if something is red and nice, it must be cold.\n12. **All round things are green.** - This implies that if something is round, it is green.\n13. **If something is nice and not cold then it is green.** - This implies that if something is nice and not cold, it is green.\n\nNow, let\'s evaluate the statement "Erin is green":.\n\n- Erin is red (from statement 2).\n- Red things are nice (from statement 7).\n- If something is red and nice, it is cold (from statement 11).\n- If something is nice and not cold, it is green (from statement 12).\n\nSince Erin is red and nice, according to statement 11, Erin must be cold. However, according to statement 12, if something is nice and not cold, it is green. Since Erin is not cold, it does not satisfy the condition of being nice and not cold. Therefore, Erin cannot be green based on the given information.\n\nThus, the statement "Erin is green" is false.\n\n<｜User｜>Please solve the logical reasoning problem. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
