ue, then it is rough.** This tells us that if something is both red and blue, it must be rough.\n12. **All blue, cold things are nice.** This tells us that if something is blue and cold, it must be nice.\n13. **All red things are blue.** This tells us that if something is red, it must be blue.\n14. **If something is round and cold, then it is blue.** This tells us that if something is round and cold, it must be blue.\n15. **Blue things are big.** This tells us that if something is blue, it must be big.\n16. **If Charlie is big, then Charlie is blue.** This tells us that if Charlie is big, it must be blue.\n\nNow, let\'s use this information to determine if Harry is blue:\n\n- We know that Harry is nice (from point 6).\n- From point 10, if something is nice, it must be cold.\n- From point 11, if something is red and blue, it must be rough.\n- From point 12, if something is blue and cold, it must be nice.\n- From point 13, if something is blue, it must be big.\n- From point 14, if something is round and cold, it must be blue.\n- From point 15, if something is blue, it must be big.\n- From point 16, if Charlie is big, it must be blue.\n\nSince Harry is nice, it must be cold (from point 10). Since Harry is round and cold, it must be blue (from point 14). Since Harry is blue, it must be big (from point 13). Since Harry is big, it must be blue (from point 16).\n\nTherefore, based on the given information, the statement "Harry is blue" is true.\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
