 young.\n- From point 15, white things are cold.\n- From point 16, all young things are nice.\n- From point 17, if Gary is nice, then Gary is young.\n- From point 18, if something is young, then it is nice.\n- From point 19, if something is furry and blue, then it is white.\n- From point 20, if something is young and furry, then it is nice.\n\nSince Charlie is blue and quiet, and we don\'t have direct information about Charlie being young, we need to consider the implications of the other statements:\n\n- If Charlie is cold, then Charlie is young (point 14).\n- If Charlie is young, then Charlie is nice (point 16).\n\nHowever, we don\'t have enough information to definitively conclude that Charlie is cold. Therefore, we cannot confirm that Charlie is young based solely on the given information.\n\nThus, the statement "Charlie is nice" is **unknown** because we do not have enough information to determine whether Charlie is young or not.\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
