 kind.\n\n11. **All cold things are kind.**.\n    - This means that if something is cold, it must also be kind.\n\n12. **If Erin is young then Erin is not quiet.**.\n    - This means that if Erin is young, she cannot be quiet.\n\n13. **If something is kind and not young then it is round.**.\n    - This means that if something is kind and not young, it must also be round.\n\nNow, let\'s use these statements to determine if Erin is cold:.\n\n- We know Erin is nice (from statement 4).\n- Since nice things are quiet (from statement 5), Erin is quiet.\n- Since quiet things are cold (from statement 8), Erin is cold.\n\nTherefore, the statement "Erin is cold" is true based on the given information.\n\n<｜User｜>Please solve the logical reasoning problem. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
