cold.**.\n    - This tells us that young people are cold.\n\n11. **If someone is quiet and nice then they are rough.**.\n    - This tells us that if someone is quiet and nice, they are rough.\n\n12. **If someone is rough and young then they are cold.**.\n    - This tells us that if someone is rough and young, they are cold.\n\n13. **All rough, nice people are big.**.\n    - This tells us that all rough, nice people are big.\n\nNow, let\'s analyze the statement "Gary is rough":.\n\n- We know that Gary is green and young.\n- According to statement 8, if someone is green and young, they are nice.\n- According to statement 9, green people are nice.\n- According to statement 10, all nice people are quiet.\n- According to statement 11, if someone is quiet and nice, they are rough.\n- Therefore, since Gary is nice, he must be rough. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
