y then Bob is smart.**.\n    - This tells us that if Bob is kind and furry, then Bob is smart.\n\n14. **If something is cold and kind then it is white.**.\n    - This tells us that if something is cold and kind, then it is white.\n\nNow, let\'s use these pieces of information to determine if Dave is white:.\n\n- We know that Dave is cold.\n- We also know that Dave is smart.\n- According to point 11, white things are kind.\n- Since Dave is cold and smart, and cold, smart things are red (point 10), Dave cannot be white because white things are kind, and Dave is not kind (point 4).\n\nTherefore, based on the given information, the statement "Dave is white" is false.\n\n<｜User｜>Please solve the logical reasoning problem. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
