mart and round, it is nice.\n\n12. **Red things are nice.**\n    - This statement implies that if something is red, it is nice.\n\n13. **Rough, nice things are round.**\n    - This statement implies that if something is both rough and nice, it is round.\n\n14. **Cold things are rough.**\n    - This statement implies that if something is cold, it is rough.\n\n15. **If something is red and nice then it is cold.**\n    - This statement implies that if something is both red and nice, it must be cold.\n\n16. **All round things are green.**\n    - This statement implies that if something is round, it is green.\n\n17. **If something is nice and not cold then it is green.**\n    - This statement implies that if something is nice and not cold, it must be green.\n\nNow, let\'s evaluate the statement "Dave is not smart" based on these statements:\n\n- We know that Dave is nice (from statement 1).\n- We know that Dave is red (from statement 2).\n- According to statement 15, all round things are green.\n- According to statement 16, if something is nice and not cold, it is green.\n- According to statement 14, if something is red and nice, it is cold.\n- Since Dave is nice and red, according to statement 14, Dave must be cold.\n- According to statement 16, if something is nice and not cold, it is green.\n- Since Dave is nice and cold, according to statement 16, Dave must be green.\n- According to statement 13, smart, round things are nice.\n- Since Dave is nice and round (from statement 2), according to statement 13, Dave must be smart.\n\nTherefore, the statement "Dave is not smart" is false based on the given information.\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
